Section eight of said Act Numbered Twenty-five hundred and seventy-three is hereby amended
to read as follows:
"Section 8. For the purposes of this Act work animals are hereby appraised as follows: carabaos, three to five
years of age, fifty to one hundred pesos; five to ten years of age, one hundred to one hundred and fifty pesos;
ten to fifteen years of age, fifty to one hundred pesos; fifteen to twenty years of age, twenty-five to fifty pesos;
over twenty years of age, no value. Work cattle, three to five years of age, fifty to ninety pesos; five to eight
years of age, eighty to one hundred and twenty pesos; eight to to twelve years of age, fifty to eighty pesos;
over twelve years of age, no value. Said Board shall arrange a schedule of values within the limits prescribed
in this section. When an animal reaches the age limit in any of the above-mentioned classes it shall
automatically pass to the succeeding class."
